            <div xml:id="d200">

                <pb facs="0838" n="809" xml:id="pg809"/>

                <head>200. Letter From Helen Cohn Needham to
                    the Deputy Under Secretary of State for Management (Read)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d200-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1978-01-26">January 26, 1978</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <salute>Dear Mr. Read:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>It has come to our attention that members of the State Department’s personnel
                    staff have been telling women Foreign Service officers that the sex
                    discrimination class actions brought on behalf of women Foreign Service
                        officers<anchor n="2" xml:id="d200-f2"/> are frivolous and without basis and
                    that class members will be ultimately liable for the Department’s attorney fees.
                    In our view these comments constitute harassment and intimidation of the class
                    members and we must insist that official action be taken to prevent further
                    improper comments. We request that you inform in writing all members of your
                    staff, that any remarks to women Foreign Service officers which could be
                    interpreted as intimidation, harassment, or otherwise suggesting that they
                    disassociate themselves from the class-action litigation must be halted
                    immediately.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#bold">Bruce J.
                                Terris</hi></item>
                            <item>
                                <hi rendition="#bold">Helen Cohn
                                        Needham</hi><anchor n="3" xml:id="d200-f3"/>
                            </item>
                        </list></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d200-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d200-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Records of the Under Secretary for Management
                    (M), 1977–1978, Box 8, Chron February 1978. No classification marking. Copies
